# Step 17: the project profile and memory, in cortex-knowledge, and what it
# added to cortex-policy (the exact rule of an accepted command, and a
# running session's learned rules), cortex-agent (section 5 of the system
# prompt, outside the epoch's base hash) and cortex-core (the epoch's
# profile in the log).
#
# Each rule is broken here: what is in use and what runs without asking,
# that a shared entry is a proposal until this user accepts it, the strict
# reading of the two files, the store's lock, its good copy and its refusal
# to write over a file a person broke, the ids that are never given twice,
# expiry, the escaping and the budget of section 5, and that a learned rule
# is one exact line that waits for trust.

# ------------------------------------------------------------- the standing

[break] an-expired-entry-is-in-use
rule: An entry past its expiry is not in use: it leaves the prompt and the safe list by the clock, before anything marks it.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/entry.rs
in: Entry::in_use
find: self.status == Status::Active && !self.is_expired(now)
replace: self.status == Status::Active
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge entry::tests::an_entry_is_in_use_only_while_active_and_before_its_expiry
    cortex-knowledge::it project::an_entry_past_its_expiry_drops_out_and_is_marked_once
    cortex-knowledge::it render::nothing_that_is_not_in_use_is_in_the_section

[break] a-proposal-is-in-use
rule: A proposed entry is never in use: it reaches the prompt only after the user accepts it.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/entry.rs
in: Entry::in_use
find: self.status == Status::Active
replace: self.status != Status::Disabled
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge entry::tests::an_entry_is_in_use_only_while_active_and_before_its_expiry
    cortex-knowledge::it project::a_proposal_waits_for_the_user
    cortex-knowledge::it project::a_shared_entry_is_a_proposal_until_this_user_accepts_it
    cortex-knowledge::it render::nothing_that_is_not_in_use_is_in_the_section

[break] an-active-command-runs-unasked-without-acceptance
rule: A command that became active by itself is in the prompt and still asks: only one the user accepted, or wrote, runs without asking.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/entry.rs
in: Entry::runs_unasked
find: self.in_use(now) && self.is_accepted()
replace: self.in_use(now)
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge entry::tests::only_an_accepted_command_in_use_runs_unasked
    cortex-knowledge::it project::only_active_entries_are_in_use_and_only_accepted_commands_run_unasked

[break] a-shared-entry-is-accepted-for-having-been-written
rule: An entry of the repository's file is never the user's word for having been written there.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/entry.rs
in: Entry::is_accepted
find: (self.scope == Scope::Private && self.learned.is_none())
replace: self.learned.is_none()
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge entry::tests::a_shared_entry_is_not_accepted_for_having_been_written

[break] a-shared-entry-is-active-until-decided
rule: A shared entry the user has not decided about is a proposal, not an active entry.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/project.rs
in: standing
find: None => entry.status = Status::Proposed
replace: None => entry.status = Status::Active
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it project::a_shared_entry_is_a_proposal_until_this_user_accepts_it
    cortex-knowledge::it project::a_shared_file_cannot_give_its_own_entries_a_standing
    cortex-knowledge::it render::nothing_that_is_not_in_use_is_in_the_section

[break] an-acceptance-outlives-a-changed-command
rule: A user's acceptance of a shared entry is of what it said: the command line is part of the hash, so a changed command is a proposal again.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/entry.rs
in: Entry::content_hash
find: part(&command.run);
replace: part("");
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge entry::tests::the_content_hash_follows_what_the_entry_says_and_nothing_else
    cortex-knowledge::it project::a_shared_entry_that_changes_is_a_proposal_again

[break] a-degraded-store-feeds-the-safe-list
rule: While the private store cannot be read as it is, the state in its place feeds the prompt and never the safe list.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/project.rs
in: Snapshot::runs_unasked
find: !degraded && entry.runs_unasked(now)
replace: (degraded || true) && entry.runs_unasked(now)
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it store::an_invalid_store_is_reported_and_never_written_over
    cortex-knowledge::it store::a_session_keeps_what_it_had_when_an_edit_goes_wrong

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the files

[break] an-unknown-key-of-the-store-is-passed-over
rule: The private store is read strictly: a key this build does not know refuses the file.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/file.rs
find: #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] struct RawPrivate
replace: struct RawPrivate
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge file::tests::a_file_this_build_does_not_understand_in_full_is_refused_whole

[break] a-shared-entry-may-carry-a-standing
rule: An entry of the shared file has no status, date or acceptance of its own: one that claims any is left out.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/file.rs
find: #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] struct RawShared
replace: struct RawShared
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge file::tests::a_shared_entry_that_claims_a_standing_is_left_out
    cortex-knowledge::it project::a_shared_file_cannot_give_its_own_entries_a_standing

[break] a-newer-version-is-read
rule: A file of a newer version is refused whole.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/file.rs
in: check_version
find: version == VERSION
replace: version >= VERSION
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge file::tests::a_file_this_build_does_not_understand_in_full_is_refused_whole
    cortex-knowledge file::tests::a_shared_file_past_its_cap_or_of_a_later_version_is_refused

[break] the-entry-cap-is-not-held
rule: A private store past its cap on entries is invalid.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/file.rs
in: parse_private
find: read.entries.len() > MAX_PRIVATE_ENTRIES
replace: false
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge file::tests::a_store_past_its_cap_is_refused

[break] an-id-is-given-again
rule: The id of a deleted entry is not given again, so a change sent from an old listing cannot land on an entry the user never saw.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/file.rs
in: PrivateState::next_number
find: self.next.max(largest_number(&self.entries) + 1)
replace: largest_number(&self.entries) + 1
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge file::tests::an_id_is_never_given_twice
    cortex-knowledge::it project::an_id_from_an_old_listing_does_not_land_on_a_new_entry

[break] a-shared-id-is-a-short-prefix
rule: A shared entry's id is 128 bits of its hash, so a repository cannot make two entries share one.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/file.rs
in: shared_id
find: hex.get(..32)
replace: hex.get(..12)
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge file::tests::every_shared_entry_is_a_proposal_named_by_what_it_says

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the store

[break] a-change-writes-over-an-invalid-store
rule: A store that cannot be read as it is, is never written over: a change is refused until a person puts the file right.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/store.rs
in: Store::change
find: self.read_strict().map_err(StoreError::Invalid)?
replace: self.read_strict().unwrap_or_default()
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it store::an_invalid_store_is_reported_and_never_written_over

[break] the-store-is-not-owner-only
rule: The private store and its good copy are written owner-only.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/store.rs
in: Store::change
find: owner_only: true
replace: owner_only: false
os: linux
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it store::a_change_is_written_owner_only_with_its_good_copy_beside_it

[break] a-change-takes-no-lock
rule: A change holds the store's lock from before its read until after its write.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/store.rs
in: Store::change
find: let _lock = private::hold_lock(&self.file).map_err(io_error)?;
replace: let _lock = private::hold_lock(&self.file).map_err(io_error).map(|_| None::<std::fs::File>)?;
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it store::a_change_holds_the_lock_while_it_writes

[break] the-good-copy-does-not-follow-a-valid-load
rule: A load that reads a valid store brings the good copy up to it, so that a later invalid edit falls back to the person's last valid one.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/store.rs
in: Store::load
find: self.keep_good_copy(&read);
replace: let _ = &read;
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it store::the_good_copy_follows_a_valid_hand_edit
    cortex-knowledge::it store::an_invalid_store_is_reported_and_never_written_over

[break] a-removed-store-keeps-its-good-copy
rule: A store that is not there has no good copy: a file made by hand afterwards cannot fall back to what was removed.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/store.rs
in: Store::keep_good_copy
find: let _ = std::fs::remove_file(&good);
replace:
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it store::a_store_that_is_removed_is_empty_and_its_good_copy_goes

# -------------------------------------------------------------- the changes

[break] a-proposal-is-stored-active
rule: A model's proposal is stored as proposed: nothing a model does can make an entry active.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/project.rs
in: Project::propose
find: entry.status = Status::Proposed;
replace: entry.status = Status::Active;
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it project::a_proposal_waits_for_the_user

[break] a-rejected-proposal-is-proposed-again
rule: A proposal the user turned down is already known, and is not stored again.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/project.rs
in: Project::propose
find: entry.kind == proposal.kind && one_spaced(&entry.text) == text
replace: entry.status != Status::Disabled && entry.kind == proposal.kind && one_spaced(&entry.text) == text
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it project::a_proposal_waits_for_the_user

[break] the-cap-on-waiting-proposals-is-not-held
rule: A store full of a model's proposals takes no more until some are reviewed.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/project.rs
in: Project::propose
find: waiting >= MAX_PENDING_PROPOSALS
replace: false
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it project::a_store_full_of_proposals_takes_no_more_until_some_are_reviewed

[break] a-lapsed-entry-keeps-its-acceptance
rule: An acceptance does not outlast the entry: a lapsed command must be accepted again before it runs without asking.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/project.rs
in: Project::lapse
find: entry.accepted = None;
replace:
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it project::an_entry_past_its_expiry_drops_out_and_is_marked_once

[break] an-unaccepted-entry-is-promoted
rule: Only an entry the user stands behind goes to the shared file.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/project.rs
in: Work::promote
find: !entry.is_accepted()
replace: false
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it project::only_an_entry_the_user_stands_behind_is_promoted
    cortex-knowledge::it project::an_update_is_all_or_nothing

[break] a-linked-cortex-directory-is-read-through
rule: The shared file is read only from a `.cortex` that is a directory of the workspace itself.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/project.rs
in: Project::read_shared
find: Ok(found) if found.file_type().is_symlink() =>
replace: Ok(found) if false && found.file_type().is_symlink() =>
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it project::a_shared_file_behind_a_link_is_not_read

[break] an-edit-reaches-a-shared-entry
rule: An entry of the shared file is edited and removed in that file, never through the user's store.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/project.rs
in: Work::not_private
find: Ok(Some(_)) => ChangeError::SharedReadOnly(id.clone())
replace: Ok(Some(_)) => ChangeError::UnknownEntry(id.clone())
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it project::an_update_is_all_or_nothing

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- section 5

[break] an-entry-is-rendered-unescaped
rule: Every piece of an entry goes through `visible`, so an entry is one list line and cannot begin a line of its own.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/render.rs
in: line
find: let text = visible(&entry.text);
replace: let text = entry.text.as_str();
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it render::no_entry_can_write_anything_but_its_own_line

[break] a-commands-directory-is-rendered-unescaped
rule: A command's directory is escaped as its text is.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/render.rs
in: line
find: visible(cwd)
replace: cwd
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it render::no_entry_can_write_anything_but_its_own_line

[break] the-section-passes-its-budget
rule: Section 5 stays inside its budget, and says how many entries it left out.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/render.rs
in: render_with
find: text.len() + cost(*kind, line, first) > room
replace: false
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it render::the_section_stays_inside_its_budget_and_says_what_it_left_out

[break] commands-are-not-first
rule: The section lists commands first, so that a cut leaves them in.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/render.rs
in: render_with
find: for kind in Kind::ALL
replace: for kind in [Kind::Fact, Kind::Flaky, Kind::Convention, Kind::Command]
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it render::the_section_lists_what_is_in_use_commands_first_in_a_fixed_order
    cortex-knowledge::it render::the_section_stays_inside_its_budget_and_says_what_it_left_out

[break] the-filter-is-not-asked
rule: An entry whose line the caller's filter refuses is left out of the section.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/render.rs
in: render_with
find: if keep(&line) {
replace: if keep(&line) || true {
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it render::an_entry_the_filter_refuses_is_left_out_and_counted

[break] the-profile-is-in-the-base-hash
rule: Section 5 is outside the epoch's base hash: a profile that changed between processes does not make a resume a new epoch.
file: crates/cortex-agent/src/context/prompt.rs
in: build
find: profile.is_some() && index == profile_at
replace: false
caught-by:
    cortex-agent context::prompt::tests::the_base_hash_leaves_the_project_profile_out

[break] the-epochs-profile-is-not-written
rule: The `epoch` entry records the hash of the profile its prompt holds.
file: crates/cortex-core/src/store.rs
in: epoch_body
find: profile: epoch.profile
replace: profile: None
caught-by:
    cortex-core store::tests::the_epochs_of_a_branch_are_placed_among_its_items

# ------------------------------------------------------ the learned safe list

[break] an-exact-rule-takes-a-wildcard
rule: The rule of an accepted command is that line and no other: a word a pattern would read as a wildcard gives no rule.
file: crates/cortex-policy/src/engine.rs
in: plain_word
find: character.is_whitespace() || matches!(character, '*' | '?' | '[' | ']')
replace: character.is_whitespace()
caught-by:
    cortex-policy::it learned::an_exact_rule_is_the_line_word_for_word_or_no_rule_at_all

[break] an-exact-rule-takes-the-first-of-two-commands
rule: A line of more than one command gives no rule.
file: crates/cortex-policy/src/engine.rs
in: exact_command_rule
find: let [part] = parts.as_slice() else
replace: let Some(part) = parts.first() else
caught-by:
    cortex-policy::it learned::an_exact_rule_is_the_line_word_for_word_or_no_rule_at_all

[break] an-exact-rule-takes-a-redirection
rule: A command with a redirection gives no rule: the pattern would not say where it writes.
file: crates/cortex-policy/src/engine.rs
in: exact_command_rule
find: !part.redirects.is_empty()
replace: false
caught-by:
    cortex-policy::it learned::an_exact_rule_is_the_line_word_for_word_or_no_rule_at_all

[break] learned-rules-are-added-to-the-ones-before
rule: A session's learned rules are replaced whole, so a command the user turned off asks again at once.
file: crates/cortex-policy/src/engine.rs
in: Engine::set_learned
find: held.configured.retain(|rule| rule.source != RuleSource::Learned);
replace:
caught-by:
    cortex-policy::it learned::an_accepted_command_no_longer_asks_and_a_rejected_one_does
    cortex-policy::it learned::learned_rules_change_nothing_else_about_the_engine

[break] a-learned-list-may-do-more-than-allow-a-command
rule: A learned rule only ever allows a command: a list with anything else is refused whole.
file: crates/cortex-policy/src/engine.rs
in: Engine::set_learned
find: rule.rule.effect != Effect::Exec || rule.rule.action != RuleAction::Allow
replace: false
caught-by:
    cortex-policy::it learned::a_learned_list_with_anything_but_an_exec_allow_leaves_none_in_force

[break] a-refused-learned-list-leaves-the-old-rules-in-force
rule: When a learned list is refused, no learned rule is in force, the ones from before included.
file: crates/cortex-policy/src/engine.rs
in: Engine::set_learned
find: self.recompile(&mut held);
replace: let _ = &mut held;
caught-by:
    cortex-policy::it learned::a_learned_list_with_anything_but_an_exec_allow_leaves_none_in_force

# ------------------------------------------- after the review of the store

[break] a-change-passes-the-size-cap
rule: The cap on the store's size is held when it is written: a change that would pass it is refused, and the store stays one every load reads.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/store.rs
in: writable
find: text.len() as u64 > MAX_FILE_BYTES
replace: false
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it store::a_change_that_would_pass_the_size_cap_is_refused_and_the_store_stays_readable

[break] the-shared-file-passes-its-size
rule: The cap on the shared file's size is held when an entry is added to it.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/file.rs
in: append_shared
find: text.len() as u64 > MAX_FILE_BYTES
replace: false
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge file::tests::an_entry_that_would_take_the_shared_file_past_its_size_is_not_added
    cortex-knowledge::it project::a_promote_that_would_pass_the_shared_files_size_is_refused

[break] a-snapshots-stamp-is-taken-after-the-lock
rule: The snapshot a change gives back holds the store's stamp from while the lock was held, so another process's change right after it shows at the next look.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/project.rs
in: Project::after
find: false, private_stamp, shared_stamp
replace: false, self.store.stamp(), shared_stamp
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it store::a_change_made_by_another_right_after_ours_is_seen

[break] a-load-waits-for-the-lock
rule: A load never waits for the store's lock: the good copy is brought up to date only when the lock can be had at once.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/store.rs
in: Store::keep_good_copy
find: let Some(_lock) = self.try_lock() else
replace: let Ok(_lock) = private::hold_lock(&self.file) else
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it store::a_load_does_not_wait_for_a_writer

[break] a-problem-quotes-the-file-raw
rule: A problem is shown to a person and sent to clients: what it quotes of the file is escaped.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/file.rs
in: Problem::new
find: cortex_base::visible(&message.into()).into_owned()
replace: message.into()
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge file::tests::a_problem_never_carries_what_acts_unseen

[break] a-left-out-entry-is-quoted-raw
rule: What is said of a shared entry that was left out is escaped too.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/file.rs
in: parse_shared
find: cortex_base::visible(&message)
replace: message
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge file::tests::a_problem_never_carries_what_acts_unseen

[break] a-number-past-the-bound-is-read
rule: A file whose id or counter holds a number past the bound is refused, so no arithmetic on it can wrap round to an id in use.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/file.rs
in: parse_private
find: largest > MAX_NUMBER || read.next.is_some_and(|next| next > MAX_NUMBER)
replace: false
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge file::tests::a_number_past_what_an_id_may_hold_refuses_the_file

[break] a-private-id-takes-a-shared-entrys-name
rule: A private entry cannot be given an id that begins `s_`: it would stand in front of a shared entry.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/file.rs
in: parse_private
find: Some(id) if id.starts_with("s_") =>
replace: Some(id) if false && id.starts_with("s_") =>
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge file::tests::a_private_id_cannot_take_a_shared_entrys_name

[break] the-shared-file-is-written-through-a-link
rule: The shared file is never written through a link, whatever the read before it found.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/project.rs
in: Project::write_shared
find: follow_links: false
replace: follow_links: true
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it project::a_link_planted_between_the_read_and_the_write_is_not_written_through

[break] a-linked-cortex-directory-is-written-into
rule: The shared file is written only into a `.cortex` that is a directory of the workspace itself.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/project.rs
in: Project::write_shared
find: found.file_type().is_symlink() || !found.is_dir()
replace: false
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it project::a_link_planted_between_the_read_and_the_write_is_not_written_through

[break] an-entry-already-shared-is-added-again
rule: A promote of an entry the shared file already holds finishes the move and adds nothing.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/project.rs
in: Work::promote
find: if !there
replace: if true
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge::it project::a_promote_that_stopped_half_way_is_finished_by_the_next

[break] a-rooted-directory-is-reread-as-relative
rule: A directory that names a root, a drive or the home directory is refused as written, never read as a path below the workspace.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/entry.rs
in: checked_dir
find: if rooted
replace: if false
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge entry::tests::a_directory_that_names_a_root_is_refused_as_written
    cortex-knowledge::it project::a_rooted_directory_is_refused_not_reread_as_a_relative_one

[break] the-hash-follows-how-a-text-is-spaced
rule: An entry's hash is of its text with its blanks made one, so a checkout that changed the line endings has the same entry.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/entry.rs
in: Entry::content_hash
find: part(&one_spaced(&self.text));
replace: part(&self.text);
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge entry::tests::the_content_hash_follows_what_the_entry_says_and_nothing_else

[break] a-check-may-hold-a-control-character
rule: A check's command and pattern are one line, with no control character.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/entry.rs
in: one_line
find: text.chars().any(char::is_control)
replace: false
caught-by:
    cortex-knowledge entry::tests::an_entry_that_is_not_well_formed_is_refused_with_the_reason

[break] a-new-entry-is-read-leniently
rule: An entry the user writes is read strictly: a field this build does not know refuses the request.
file: crates/cortex-protocol/src/project.rs
find: #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] pub struct NewEntry
replace: pub struct NewEntry
caught-by:
    cortex-protocol tests::the_golden_values_round_trip_exactly

[break] a-new-entrys-command-is-read-leniently
rule: The command of an entry the user writes is read strictly too.
file: crates/cortex-protocol/src/project.rs
find: #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] pub struct NewCommand
replace: pub struct NewCommand
caught-by:
    cortex-protocol tests::the_golden_values_round_trip_exactly

# ---------------------------------------- after the second read of the store

[break] a-promote-writes-the-shared-file-before-the-store-is-known-to-fit
rule: A promote is all or nothing: a store that could not take the change refuses it before the repository's file is written.
file: crates/cortex-knowledge/src/project.rs
in: Project::update
