[break] a-command-that-only-became-active-is-listed-as-accepted
rule: The listing says of a command whether it asks: one that became active by itself is not accepted.
file: crates/cortex-cli/src/project_view.rs
in: standing
find: EntryStatus::Active if accepted(entry) =>
replace: EntryStatus::Active if true =>
caught-by:
    cortex-cli::bin/cortex project_view::tests::the_listing_says_what_each_entry_is_and_where_it_came_from

[break] a-shared-entry-is-accepted-because-someone-wrote-it
rule: An entry of the repository's file is this user's only once accepted, whoever wrote it.
file: crates/cortex-cli/src/project_view.rs
in: accepted
find: entry.scope == EntryScope::Private && entry.source.kind == EntrySourceKind::User
replace: entry.source.kind == EntrySourceKind::User
caught-by:
    cortex-cli::bin/cortex project_view::tests::a_command_the_user_wrote_is_accepted

[break] accept-shared-accepts-the-models-proposals-too
rule: `accept --shared` accepts the repository's entries that wait, and not a proposal of the user's own store or an entry the user turned off.
file: crates/cortex-cli/src/project_view.rs
in: waiting_shared
find: entry.scope == EntryScope::Shared && entry.status == EntryStatus::Proposed
replace: entry.status != EntryStatus::Active
caught-by:
    cortex-cli::bin/cortex project_view::tests::accepting_the_shared_entries_takes_the_repositorys_proposals_and_nothing_else

[break] the-command-line-skips-the-operations-check
